# Log in through Identity first (InvoiceTracker.Identity.Api.http) and paste the accessToken here.
# Invoicing checks the customer with the Business API, so run Business too and use one of its customer ids.
@Invoicing_HostAddress = http://localhost:5073
@accessToken = paste-access-token-here
@customerId = paste-customer-id-here
@invoiceId = paste-invoice-id-here
@version = paste-version-here

### Create a draft
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "paymentTermsDays": 30,
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Call-out fee", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 450.00, "vatRate": 0.15 },
    { "description": "Labour (hours)", "quantity": 2.5, "unitPrice": 380.00, "vatRate": 0.15 },
    { "description": "Rounding check", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 0.03, "vatRate": 0.15 }
  ]
}

### List invoices (newest first)
GET {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### List drafts for one customer
GET {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices?status=Draft&customerId={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Read one invoice with lines, payments and timeline
GET {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Edit the draft (send the version from the last read)
PUT {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "paymentTermsDays": 14,
  "version": "{{version}}",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Call-out fee", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 450.00, "vatRate": 0.15 },
    { "description": "Geyser element", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 1299.99, "vatRate": 0.15 }
  ]
}

### Send it: number, issue date and due date are set
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Send again: 409, only a draft can be sent
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Delete a sent invoice: 409
DELETE {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Too many decimals: 400 with lines[0].unitPrice
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "{{customerId}}",
  "lines": [
    { "description": "Bad price", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 10.005 }
  ]
}

### Unknown or another business's customer: 400 on customerId
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/invoices
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
  "lines": []
}

### Dashboard tiles for the caller's business
GET {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/dashboard
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Run the overdue scan now for your business (Owner only)
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/admin/jobs/overdue-scan
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Run it as if today were a later date, to see the 7-day and 14-day reminders (needs OverdueScan:AllowAsOfOverride)
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/admin/jobs/overdue-scan?asOf=2026-12-20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Payment webhook without a signature is refused with 401.
### Send a signed one with scripts/simulate-payment.ps1, which computes the HMAC.
POST {{Invoicing_HostAddress}}/api/v1/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "eventId": "evt_unsigned",
  "eventType": "payment.succeeded",
  "invoiceId": "{{invoiceId}}",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "ZAR"
}
